-      "statement": "Given any money mutation, when a dashboard, CLI, scheduler, public projection, or runner stage requests it, then one CycleRepository and policy engine are the sole authority for state and every client uses its durable transitions. A provider attempt is write-ahead PREPARED, then NOT_SENT for a pre-call failure with no provider contact and retry permission, SENT_UNKNOWN for post-send ambiguity with observation only, or RESPONSE_RECORDED followed by RECONCILED. A card-level buyback, open, or epic-gate hold creates an attributed HeldPosition `{positionId, cycleId, packId, memo, mint, cardRef, costMicroUsdg, insuredValue, reason, terminalState, evidenceDigest, openedAtMs, ownerDecision, resolution}`; `insuredValue` is a typed amount or null. A card attempt that remains SENT_UNKNOWN past `unresolvedCardDeadlineMinutes` (default 30, minimum 5, maximum 1440) opens the same kind of position. A position stores its configured USDG control value as a verified insured amount only when that amount is already the configured USDG asset; otherwise it stores the attributed purchase cost. It never converts a Solana stablecoin insured value without a frozen quote binding. It remains in its own custody bucket while the cycle retains only settled cards, and a cycle may become COMPLETED with open positions, including an all-held cycle with zero proceeds and a zero payout manifest. COMPLETED retains open positions for supplementary recovery; `readActiveCycle` skips it for scheduler admission, but it remains an active DurableCycleStore entry until position resolution. The 16-entry store supports the default `maxHeldPositions` 10 when positions span completed cycles; a configuration above that verified-safe value of 10 is refused at admission until post-completion position archival or a measured store-capacity exemption exists. The first accepted `sell` decision for a position atomically creates exactly one supplementary settlement keyed by `positionId`; an exact replay